WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:10.240
Introducing Prevail with Total Round Control from&nbsp;
Franklin Armory. With Total Round Control or TRC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:16.080
each and every cartridge is controlled by a&nbsp;
new, patented bolt-action system. From feeding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:22.800
all the way through to ejection, leaving&nbsp;
nothing to chance. The TRC process begins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:29.280
as a round is stripped from the magazine.&nbsp;
Dual feed guides located at the bottom of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:37.760
the bolt face direct the cartridge rim&nbsp;
up and securely under the extractor.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.960
As the TRC bolt control feeds the&nbsp;
round completely into the chamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:49.200
the rim of the cartridge activates&nbsp;
a lifter in the bolt head.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:55.920
The lifter releases TRC's automatic ejector to&nbsp;
place pressure against the rear of the case.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.760
If the magazine is empty, a single round can be&nbsp;
conveniently loaded through Prevail's receiver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:11.520
ejection port. TRC's extractor is designed&nbsp;
to effortlessly snap over the case rim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:18.960
allowing the auto ejector to be activated as&nbsp;
the round is fully locked into battery. Under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:28.160
either feeding scenario, TRC's three lug bolt&nbsp;
can now be locked into battery for safe firing.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:33.200
After firing, TRC's dual&nbsp;
cocking cams and 60° throw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:41.360
make for a quick and easy unlocking of the&nbsp;
bolt. This rotating movement also initiates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:47.360
primary extraction of the fired round. As&nbsp;
the bolt is pulled rearward to the point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.400
where the mouth of the spent case clears&nbsp;
the front of the ejection port, the auto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.400 --> 00:02:09.120
ejector expels the case clear of the receiver,&nbsp;
reliably and consistently each and every time.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:15.040
Completing the bolt's natural travel to the rear&nbsp;
allows for a spring-assisted pawl to pop around to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:21.520
the front of the retractor in the interchangeable&nbsp;
bolt head. As the bolt is again pushed forward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:27.680
the pawl engages the retractor to reset&nbsp;
the auto ejector, clearing the way for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:38.320
you to repeat the TRC cycle. The all-new Prevail&nbsp;
with Total Round Control from Franklin Armory.

